{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NDLRxR1bdiWJ35JNvxtCdJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.2-uc002-paste\n     2→title: \"Merge lines of files side by side via paste\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go paste binary on two or more files. The binary reads one line\n     6→  from each file per output cycle and joins them with a delimiter, producing merged\n     7→  columnar output. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the\n     8→  Homebrew reference binary (gpaste from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms\n     9→  that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd027-paste.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/paste.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go paste binary on two files.\n    21→      Example: paste file1.txt file2.txt\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/paste opens all input files simultaneously. On each cycle it reads one line from\n    25→      each open file, joins the lines with the delimiter, and writes the result plus a\n    26→      newline to stdout.\n    27→  - id: F3\n    28→    step: |\n    29→      When one file is exhausted, cmd/paste contributes an empty field for that file's\n    30→      column until all files are exhausted.\n    31→  - id: F4\n    32→    step: |\n    33→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/paste and\n    34→      gpaste with the same file arguments and environment.\n    35→  - id: F5\n    36→    step: |\n    37→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    38→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    39→  - id: F6\n    40→    step: |\n    41→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    42→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    43→\n    44→touchpoints:\n    45→  - T1: \"cmd/paste — parallel file merge, delimiter cycling, serial mode, unequal-length file handling (prd027-paste R1, R2, R3)\"\n    46→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    47→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    48→\n    49→success_criteria:\n    50→  - id: S1\n    51→    criterion: cmd/paste compiles and ./bin/paste exists after mage build.\n    52→  - id: S2\n    53→    criterion: The differential test for two-file parallel merge passes; lines are joined with tab, matching gpaste.\n    54→  - id: S3\n    55→    criterion: The differential test for -d with a custom delimiter passes; output uses the specified delimiter.\n    56→  - id: S4\n    57→    criterion: The differential test for unequal file lengths passes; exhausted files contribute empty fields.\n    58→  - id: S5\n    59→    criterion: The differential test for -s serial mode passes; all lines of each file are joined on one output line.\n    60→  - id: S6\n    61→    criterion: The differential test for \"-\" (stdin) as a filename passes.\n    62→\n    63→out_of_scope:\n    64→  - Files larger than available file descriptors are not a concern; paste opens all files simultaneously.\n    65→  - Multi-byte delimiter escape sequences beyond the defined set are not tested.\n    66→\n    67→test_suite: test-rel05.2\n    68→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8cc92e92-4320-4730-860e-38fed7bca8cc","uuid":"2a6bdae9-6f77-434c-b678-a42908c69c45","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/355/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.2-uc002-paste.yaml","content":"id: rel05.2-uc002-paste\ntitle: \"Merge lines of files side by side via paste\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go paste binary on two or more files. The binary reads one line\n  from each file per output cycle and joins them with a delimiter, producing merged\n  columnar output. The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the\n  Homebrew reference binary (gpaste from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms\n  that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd027-paste.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/paste.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go paste binary on two files.\n      Example: paste file1.txt file2.txt\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/paste opens all input files simultaneously. On each cycle it reads one line from\n      each open file, joins the lines with the delimiter, and writes the result plus a\n      newline to stdout.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      When one file is exhausted, cmd/paste contributes an empty field for that file's\n      column until all files are exhausted.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/paste and\n      gpaste with the same file arguments and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/paste — parallel file merge, delimiter cycling, serial mode, unequal-length file handling (prd027-paste R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/paste compiles and ./bin/paste exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for two-file parallel merge passes; lines are joined with tab, matching gpaste.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for -d with a custom delimiter passes; output uses the specified delimiter.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for unequal file lengths passes; exhausted files contribute empty fields.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for -s serial mode passes; all lines of each file are joined on one output line.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for \"-\" (stdin) as a filename passes.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - Files larger than available file descriptors are not a concern; paste opens all files simultaneously.\n  - Multi-byte delimiter escape sequences beyond the defined set are not tested.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.2\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}}}
