{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DsL2XJotwTdXm7Aeu9qV7u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementation complete. Here's a summary:\n\n**cmd/paste/main.go** — Implements prd027-paste R1-R4:\n- **R1 (Parallel merge)**: Reads one line from each input file per output line, joins with delimiter. Exhausted files contribute empty fields until all inputs are done.\n- **R2 (Delimiter config)**: `-d` accepts a delimiter list with cycling and backslash escapes (`\\n`, `\\t`, `\\\\`, `\\0`). Default is TAB.\n- **R3 (Serial mode)**: `-s` joins all lines of each file into one output line, cycling delimiters across fields.\n- **R4 (Exit codes/SIGPIPE)**: Exit 0 on success, exit 1 on error with stderr diagnostic. Calls `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`.\n\n**cmd/paste/paste_test.go** — Differential tests against `gpaste`:\n- 11 test cases covering: parallel merge, custom delimiter, serial mode, unequal lengths, stdin via `-`, delimiter cycling, empty files, serial delimiter cycling, backslash escapes.\n- Gracefully skips when `gpaste` is not in PATH (D4).\n\n**Acceptance criteria verified:**\n- AC1: Compiles with no errors\n- AC2: Parallel merge joins with TAB (verified manually)\n- AC3: Serial mode joins all lines of each file\n- AC4: Delimiter cycling works with multi-char lists and escapes\n- AC5: Stdin handled as `-` operand and as default\n- AC6: Tests pass (skip gracefully without gpaste)\n- AC7: Exit 0 on success, 1 on error"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":214,"cache_read_input_tokens":64822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":214},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8cc92e92-4320-4730-860e-38fed7bca8cc","uuid":"ec8d51e8-cad9-45ef-8ddc-09da687c3185"}
